From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Yocom <630234+danyocom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:10:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] Support the in-game reset in Diddy Kong Racing DS

The game uses the stock interrupt dispatcher up to the acknowledge and then
dispatches differently: the handler is loaded into r2 rather than r0, and both
the push of lr and the load of the return address are skipped for interrupt 10,
so that handler is entered with no return address at all. The stock signature
cannot match, and in fact the whole arm9 binary contains no "bx r0".

The jump replaces the conditional return address load and the call, so the push
has already happened and the flags still say whether this is the interrupt that
skips it. Setting lr for that one would send its handler to a return address
with nothing pushed to match, so it is left holding the return into the BIOS.

This dispatcher also enters handlers with the interrupt index in r0 rather than
the handler address, so the dispatch part leaves r0 alone. On the vblank path,
where the key check and the reset need r2 and overwrite r0, the handler is kept
in a word of the patch and a small stub restores it along with the index, which
is always zero there.
